# SR10: the four-card platform replay of the PRODUCTION image: the node agent's serving sequence in a copy of its container running the production THIN LAYER (@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@, filled in by the private driver with the image production runs now,
# already in the rig's Docker daemon; this public template carries only the placeholder) on the production ENGINE (the base image tp4-serve-10 under it). The replay sets the production profile BY NAME. READ the vLLM subprocess log from the container (never docker logs):
# '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix: vLLM argv', the P150x4 mesh, the extent block, the request-warm line BEFORE the block capture, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED, prefix installed, the prefill warm checks; the :tt alias advertised before and after the restart.
# Pass: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True' plus the thinking-budget smoke (C2_REPLAY_BUDGET_SMOKE=1, up to 90 min, fails the job if it ran and failed); its one long prompt must answer long and untruncated. The replay turns the session cap OFF. The restart step is the first reopening of the mesh after an unclean exit:
# a wedge FAILS the replay. SALT: c2_platform_replay.py sends NO cache_salt, so SR10 cannot read a sticky admit with reused tokens > 0; the operator's salted two-turn check after the release covers that. Measured real time about 25 min; the workflow's replay step is killed at 180 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE EXTENSION window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-ext and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The extension runs ONLY on today's production ENGINE: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's; production's thin layer on top of it is NOT exercised
# except in SR10, which replays it) and the production profile family c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix
C2_REPLAY_BUDGET_SMOKE=1
